  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Clear work. Quiet surfaces.",
    "overview": "This document describes the completed [standalone design sheet](index.html), a quieter composition proposal selected by the user. The familiar blue, neutral surfaces, bilingual type and visible controls support warehouse tasks and people operations. Headings, spacing and a small number of dividers provide hierarchy; related work shares a surface.\n\n**Scope and authority:** the frontmatter is normative only for this sheet. It records the palette extracted at the start of the 2026-10-09 session, as preserved in [tokens.css](tokens.css), and the typography, shapes and component values implemented in [styles.css](styles.css). The `badge-*` colors are explicitly proposed foreground additions from the final stylesheet, requested for stronger status contrast; they are not part of the original token extraction. The proposed layout rules below are reviewable recommendations, not shipped application rules. This file does not create or replace project-wide design authority. [README.md](README.md) maps every specimen to its application sources.\n\n**Current extracted tokens and working-tree drift:** at documentation time, `src/app/globals.css` has a different light-theme blue, canvas, text, raised surface, muted text and several semantic/hover values. For example, its blue is `#1d4ed8`, canvas is `#ffffff`, text is `#17212f`, raised surface is `#f6f7f9`, and muted text is `#475569`. Those current working-tree values are not the sheet's session snapshot. The sheet remains a composition proposal; it does not authorize a palette migration or revert other work. The current application stylesheet owns current application tokens.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Familiar blue for primary action, with neutral secondary controls.",
      "One task surface with divided sections and unboxed totals.",
      "Thai and English, fixed operating type sizes and numeric clarity.",
      "Distinct status, loading, empty and failed-save presentations."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Meaningful Color Rule",
        "body": "Pair status color with an icon and readable text. Preserve area identity separately from selection, occupancy and status.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Numeric Identity Rule",
        "body": "Use monospace for codes, times and measurements, and tabular figures for aligned quantities. Preserve natural Thai wrapping.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Task Surface Rule",
        "body": "Within this proposal, group with spacing and selective dividers before adding another container. Keep a surface when it defines a workspace or map boundary.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Task Rule",
        "body": "Keep task content flat in this proposal. Use surface tone and hierarchy to separate content, reserving borders for controls, boundaries and meaningful divisions.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Scoped Action Rule",
        "body": "Give each task one primary next action, and keep secondary actions neutral.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve the familiar palette roles, bilingual fonts and visible control boundaries when reviewing this composition.",
      "**Do** group related work with headings, spacing and selective dividers inside the shared task surface.",
      "**Do** keep field labels 2px above inputs, with AI origin beside the field name as requested for this proposal.",
      "**Do** pair status color with text and an icon, and keep physical area identity separate.",
      "**Do** keep planned and actual attendance times separately labeled, and make save scope clear.",
      "**Do** check Thai and English, both themes, keyboard focus, narrow layouts, reduced motion and long identifiers before implementing a proposal."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** treat this sheet or its session token snapshot as shipped application behavior or project-wide design authority.",
      "**Don't** add repeated nested cards or boxed totals to the quieter specimens merely to group related content.",
      "**Don't** replace neutral fields with broad AI-origin color fills in this proposal.",
      "**Don't** confuse synthetic local specimen actions with backend writes, scanning, authorization or persisted attendance receipts."
    ]
  }
